      "options": {
       "html": "<!DOCTYPE html PUBLIC \"-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0 Transitional//EN\" \"http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/loose.dtd\">\n<html><head><meta charset=\"UTF-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\r\n<title></title>\r\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"How rent-to-own really works in Loveland, Fort Collins &amp; Northern Colorado in 2026 &mdash; plus the scams to avoid and the $0-down programs most renters don't know they qualify for.\"><meta name=\"author\" content=\"Christine Gwinnup\">\r\n<link href=\"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com/rent-to-own\" rel=\"canonical\"><meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index,follow,max-image-preview:large\"><!-- Open Graph --><meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\"><meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Rent-to-Own Homes in Northern Colorado: An Honest 2026 Guide\"><meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"How rent-to-own really works in Loveland, Fort Collins &amp; Northern Colorado in 2026 &mdash; plus the scams to avoid and the $0-down programs most renters don't know they qualify for.\"><meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com/rent-to-own\"><meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://idx-acnt-ihouseprd.b-cdn.net/AR1140900/file_manager/Screenshot%202025-11-10%20at%2012.48.32%E2%80%AFPM.png\"><meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"The Little Lady Sells Homes\"><meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\"><!-- Twitter Card --><meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\"><meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Rent-to-Own Homes in Northern Colorado: An Honest 2026 Guide\"><meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\"How rent-to-own really works in Loveland, Fort Collins &amp; Northern Colorado in 2026 &mdash; plus the scams to avoid and the $0-down programs most renters don't know they qualify for.\"><meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://idx-acnt-ihouseprd.b-cdn.net/AR1140900/file_manager/Screenshot%202025-11-10%20at%2012.48.32%E2%80%AFPM.png\"><!-- Font preconnect -->\r\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\" rel=\"preconnect\">\r\n<link crossorigin=\"\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" rel=\"preconnect\">\r\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,500;0,9..144,600;0,9..144,700;1,9..144,400&amp;family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&amp;display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\r\n<link crossorigin=\"\" href=\"https://form.jotform.com\" rel=\"preconnect\"><!-- Complete Schema including WebPage --><script type=\"application/ld+json\">\r\n  {\r\n    \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\r\n    \"@graph\": [\r\n      {\r\n        \"@type\": \"WebPage\",\r\n        \"@id\": \"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com/rent-to-own\",\r\n        \"url\": \"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com/rent-to-own\",\r\n        \"name\": \"Rent-to-Own Homes in Northern Colorado: An Honest 2026 Guide\",\r\n        \"description\": \"How rent-to-own really works in Loveland, Fort Collins & Northern Colorado in 2026 — plus the scams to avoid and the $0-down programs most renters don't know they qualify for.\",\r\n        \"datePublished\": \"2026-04-13\",\r\n        \"dateModified\": \"2026-04-13\",\r\n        \"primaryImageOfPage\": {\r\n          \"@type\": \"ImageObject\",\r\n          \"url\": \"https://idx-acnt-ihouseprd.b-cdn.net/AR1140900/file_manager/Screenshot%202025-11-10%20at%2012.48.32%E2%80%AFPM.png\"\r\n        }\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"@type\": \"RealEstateAgent\",\r\n        \"@id\": \"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com/#agent\",\r\n        \"name\": \"Christine Gwinnup - The Little Lady Sells Homes\",\r\n        \"image\": \"https://idx-acnt-ihouseprd.b-cdn.net/AR1140900/file_manager/Screenshot%202025-11-10%20at%2012.48.32%E2%80%AFPM.png\",\r\n        \"telephone\": \"+1-303-709-4262\",\r\n        \"url\": \"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com\",\r\n        \"areaServed\": [\"Loveland\", \"Fort Collins\", \"Greeley\", \"Windsor\"],\r\n        \"knowsAbout\": [\"Rent to own homes Colorado\", \"First time home buyer programs Colorado\", \"USDA loans Colorado\", \"CHFA programs Colorado\"]\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"@type\": \"Service\",\r\n        \"serviceType\": \"Homeownership Eligibility Assessment\",\r\n        \"provider\": { \"@id\": \"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com/#agent\" },\r\n        \"areaServed\": [\"Loveland\", \"Fort Collins\", \"Greeley\", \"Windsor\"],\r\n        \"offers\": { \"@type\": \"Offer\", \"price\": \"0\", \"priceCurrency\": \"USD\", \"description\": \"Free 60-second path check\" }\r\n      },\r\n      {\r\n        \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\r\n        \"mainEntity\": [\r\n          {\r\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n            \"name\": \"Are rent-to-own homes legit in Colorado?\",\r\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Some are, but most online rent-to-own listings for Northern Colorado are either lead-generation traps, pre-foreclosure situations, or expensive corporate programs. Always verify with a local Realtor before any money changes hands.\" }\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n            \"name\": \"How does rent-to-own work in Loveland and Fort Collins?\",\r\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"A rent-to-own agreement in Loveland or Fort Collins typically involves leasing a home for 1–3 years with the right or obligation to buy at the end. A portion of your monthly rent goes toward your future down payment.\" }\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n            \"name\": \"Do I need good credit for rent-to-own in Colorado?\",\r\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Most legitimate programs require a credit score of at least 580–620, verifiable income of roughly 3x the monthly rent, and no recent evictions or bankruptcies.\" }\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n            \"name\": \"What's the difference between lease-option and lease-purchase in Colorado?\",\r\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"A lease-option gives you the right but not the obligation to buy. A lease-purchase creates a contractual obligation to buy — and if you can't qualify for a mortgage at the end, you can be sued for breach of contract.\" }\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n            \"name\": \"Can I rent-to-own with bad credit in Northern Colorado?\",\r\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Most legitimate programs still require a 580+ credit score. If your credit is lower, the honest answer is that no rent-to-own program will be a good deal for you — and 12 months of focused credit repair will get you further than a lease-option ever will.\" }\r\n          },\r\n          {\r\n            \"@type\": \"Question\",\r\n            \"name\": \"Are there alternatives to rent-to-own that get me into a home faster?\",\r\n            \"acceptedAnswer\": { \"@type\": \"Answer\", \"text\": \"Yes — and most renters who call about rent-to-own actually qualify for one. CHFA offers down payment assistance grants. USDA loans offer $0 down in much of Weld County. FHA with down payment assistance often requires nothing out of pocket.\" }\r\n          }\r\n        ]\r\n      }\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n  </script>\r\n<style type=\"text/css\">* { box-sizing: border-box; }\r\n    html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }\r\n    :root { --forest:#1f3a2e; --gold:#b98e4d; --ivory:#fbf7f1; --line:#e4dccf; --radius:18px; }\r\n    body { margin:0; font-family:Inter,system-ui,sans-serif; background:var(--ivory); color:#1b1f1c; line-height:1.7; }\r\n    .container { max-width:1140px; margin:0 auto; padding:0 24px; }\r\n    iframe { width:100%; min-height:620px; border:none; border-radius:14px; }\r\n\r\n    /* Larger, more noticeable CTA button */\r\n    .nav-cta {\r\n      background:#1f3a2e;\r\n      color:white;\r\n      padding:18px 36px;\r\n      border-radius:9999px;\r\n      text-decoration:none;\r\n      font-weight:700;\r\n      font-size:1.15rem;\r\n      box-shadow:0 10px 30px -10px rgba(31,58,46,.5);\r\n      transition:all .2s ease;\r\n    }\r\n    .nav-cta:hover {\r\n      transform:scale(1.05);\r\n      box-shadow:0 14px 35px -10px rgba(31,58,46,.6);\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    /* Scroll margin to clear sticky header on anchor links */\r\n    #guide, #faqs, #quick-check {\r\n      scroll-margin-top: 90px;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    @media (max-width:720px) {\r\n      .container { padding:0 16px; }\r\n      .hero-inner { grid-template-columns:1fr !important; }\r\n      .quick-check-inner { grid-template-columns:1fr !important; }\r\n      iframe { min-height:560px; }\r\n    }\r\n</style>\r\n<!-- HEADER -->\r\n<header style=\"position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 50; background: rgba(251,247,241,.95); backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line)\">\r\n<div class=\"container\" style=\"min-height:78px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:12px;\"><a href=\"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com\" style=\"display:flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; text-decoration:none;\">\r\n<div style=\"width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--forest); color: white; display: grid; place-items: center; font-family: Georgia,serif; font-style: italic; font-weight: 700\">ll</div>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>The Little Lady</strong><br>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:0.8rem;letter-spacing:1px;\">303-709-4262</span></div>\r\n</a>\r\n\r\n<nav aria-label=\"Primary navigation\"><a href=\"#guide\" style=\"margin-right:20px;\">Guide</a> <a href=\"#faqs\" style=\"margin-right:20px;\">FAQs</a> <a class=\"nav-cta\" href=\"#quick-check\">See My Best Path to Getting You Home</a></nav>\r\n</div>\r\n</header>\r\n\r\n<main id=\"main-content\"><!-- HERO -->\r\n<section style=\"padding: 60px 0; background: linear-gradient(180deg,#f8f1e4 0%,var(--ivory) 100%)\">\r\n<div class=\"container hero-inner\" style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 340px;gap:48px;align-items:center;\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div style=\"background: #b98e4d; color: white; padding: 7px 14px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 800; display: inline-flex\">Loveland &middot; Fort Collins &middot; Greeley &middot; Windsor &middot; Northern Colorado</div>\r\n\r\n<h1 style=\"font-size:clamp(2.6rem,5vw,4.8rem);font-family:Georgia,serif;\">Rent-to-Own Homes in Northern Colorado: An Honest 2026 Guide</h1>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;margin-top:24px;\">\r\n<div><strong>25+</strong><br>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:0.9rem;color:#5a625d;\">Years in NoCo</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>150+</strong><br>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:0.9rem;color:#5a625d;\">Families helped</span></div>\r\n\r\n<div><strong>100+</strong><br>\r\n<span style=\"font-size:0.9rem;color:#5a625d;\">5-star reviews</span></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 32px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 0 20px 60px -24px rgba(31,58,46,.24)\"><img alt=\"Christine Gwinnup, Northern Colorado Realtor specializing in Rent-to-Own and $0-Down programs\" fetchpriority=\"high\" height=\"110\" src=\"https://idx-acnt-ihouseprd.b-cdn.net/AR1140900/file_manager/Screenshot%202025-11-10%20at%2012.48.32%E2%80%AFPM.png\" style=\"border-radius:50%;object-fit:cover;border:4px solid white;\" width=\"110\">\r\n<div style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:1.55rem;color:var(--forest);\">Christine Gwinnup</div>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"color:#5a625d;\">Northern Colorado Realtor</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n<!-- QUICK SUMMARY BOX + APRIL 2026 LOCAL NOTE -->\r\n\r\n<div class=\"container\" style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 24px; margin: 24px auto; box-shadow: 0 20px 60px -24px rgba(31,58,46,.24); max-width: 1140px\">\r\n<h3 style=\"margin-top:0; font-size:1.1rem; color:var(--forest);\">Quick Summary for NoCo Renters:</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul style=\"margin:0; padding-left:20px; display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr)); gap:10px; font-size:0.95rem;\">\r\n\t<li><strong>Best Locations:</strong> Weld County (Greeley) has more inventory than Larimer.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Credit Score:</strong> Legitimate programs typically require <strong>580&ndash;620+</strong>.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Most renters I talk to are surprised they qualify for programs like $0-down USDA or CHFA.</strong></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:16px; font-size:0.95rem; color:#5a625d; font-style:italic;\"><strong>April 2026 Local Note:</strong> We are seeing more $0-down USDA approvals in the Promontory area of Greeley than anywhere else in NoCo right now.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<!-- GUIDE SECTION -->\r\n\r\n<article class=\"container\" id=\"guide\" style=\"padding:60px 0;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-style:italic;color:#5a625d;margin-bottom:24px;\"><strong>By <a href=\"https://www.thelittleladysellshomes.com/#agent\" style=\"color:inherit;text-decoration:none;\">Christine Gwinnup</a></strong>, Loveland Realtor &mdash; &ldquo;The Little Lady Sells Homes&rdquo;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>If you typed \"rent to own homes Loveland\" or \"rent to own homes Fort Collins\" into Google, I'm guessing one of two things is true. Either you're tired of renting and you're looking for any door into homeownership that doesn't require a perfect credit score and 20% down &mdash; or you saw a listing online that said \"rent-to-own\" and you want to know if it's real before you call the number.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I'm going to answer both honestly, because I've seen rent-to-own change a few lives &mdash; and I've seen it cost people their savings. You deserve the truth before the sales pitch.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How Does Rent-to-Own Actually Work in Colorado?</h2>\r\n\r\n<dl style=\"margin:2em 0; border-left:3px solid var(--gold); padding-left:24px;\">\r\n\t<dt style=\"font-weight:700; color:var(--forest); font-size:1.15rem;\">Lease-Option</dt>\r\n\t<dd style=\"margin:0 0 1.5em; color:#4b544d;\">Gives you the right but not the obligation to buy at the end of the lease. If you walk away, you lose the option fee and rent credits.</dd>\r\n\t<dt style=\"font-weight:700; color:var(--forest); font-size:1.15rem;\">Lease-Purchase</dt>\r\n\t<dd style=\"margin:0; color:#4b544d;\">You're contractually obligated to buy at the end. If you can't qualify for a mortgage when the time comes, you can be sued for breach of contract.</dd>\r\n</dl>\r\n<!-- SCAM ALERT BOX -->\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background: #fff0f0; border: 2px solid #b14a3f; border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 24px; margin: 32px 0\">\r\n<h3 style=\"color: #b14a3f; margin-top: 0;\"><span aria-label=\"Warning\" role=\"img\">⚠️</span> 3 Red Flags of a NoCo Rent-to-Own Scam</h3>\r\n\r\n<ul style=\"margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;\">\r\n\t<li><strong>Upfront wire transfers:</strong> Legitimate sellers won't ask for \"option fees\" before a tour.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>No proof of ownership:</strong> If they can't show a title report, walk away.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Resistance to legal review:</strong> Legitimate contracts always allow for a real estate attorney's eyes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2>Are Rent-to-Own Homes Legit in Northern Colorado?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Some are. Most aren't. I'll be the local Realtor who says it out loud: the majority of \"rent-to-own\" listings you'll find on national sites for Loveland, Fort Collins, and Greeley fall into one of three buckets:</p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n\t<li><strong>Lead-generation traps.</strong> The \"listing\" isn't a real home. It's bait to get your email and phone number, which then gets sold to credit-repair companies and mortgage lenders.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Pre-foreclosures dressed up.</strong> The \"owner\" is behind on their mortgage and trying to collect rent from you while the bank is already moving to take the house. You can lose every dollar you put in.</li>\r\n\t<li><strong>Legitimate but expensive corporate programs.</strong> Companies like Home Partners of America are real, but you typically pay above-market rent and an above-market purchase price for the convenience. Sometimes it's worth it. Often it isn't.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<h2>Do I Need Good Credit for Rent-to-Own in Colorado?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Less than you'd need for a conventional mortgage, but more than zero. Most legitimate rent-to-own programs in Northern Colorado want to see a credit score of at least 580&ndash;620, verifiable income of roughly 3x the monthly rent, and no recent evictions or bankruptcies. If your credit is below 580, rent-to-own probably isn't the right path &mdash; and the honest answer is that 12 months of focused credit repair will get you further than a lease-option ever will.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>Rent-to-Own in Loveland vs. Fort Collins vs. Greeley: What's Different?</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Larimer County (Loveland, Fort Collins, Berthoud, Wellington) and Weld County (Greeley, Windsor, Johnstown, Severance) have very different rent-to-own landscapes in 2026:</p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:18px;margin:24px 0;\">\r\n<div style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 22px\">\r\n<h3>Loveland &amp; Fort Collins</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Tight inventory, strong appreciation, very few willing seller-financers. Most \"rent-to-own\" listings here are corporate program homes or scams. Real lease-option deals usually come from off-market situations I create directly with sellers.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 22px\">\r\n<h3>Greeley &amp; Evans</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>More motivated sellers, more legitimate seller-finance opportunities, and lower entry prices. If rent-to-own is going to work for you in NoCo, this is where it's most likely to happen.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 22px\">\r\n<h3>Windsor, Johnstown, Severance</h3>\r\n\r\n<p>Mixed. Newer construction skews against rent-to-own; older neighborhoods occasionally produce real opportunities.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<h2>What Most Renters Don't Know: You Might Already Qualify to Buy</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Here's the part that surprises almost every renter I talk to. Most renters who call me asking about rent-to-own actually qualify today for a program that gets them into a home faster, with less money down, and without the lease-option markup. Programs like CHFA down payment assistance, USDA $0-down loans in Weld County, and FHA with seller credits or grants.</p>\r\n\r\n<h2>How I Help &mdash; and When I Tell People No</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>If rent-to-own is genuinely your best path, I'll help you find a legitimate one &mdash; usually by approaching specific sellers directly rather than chasing online listings. If a faster, cheaper path exists for your situation, I'll point you to it even though I make less money that way. And if the honest answer is &ldquo;spend the next 9 months fixing your credit,&rdquo; I'll say that too.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>No pressure. No upsell. Just the truth about what's actually available in Northern Colorado in 2026.</strong></p>\r\n<!-- Christine’s Promise Bar -->\r\n\r\n<div style=\"background: #f4ede2; padding: 16px; border-radius: 12px; text-align: center; margin: 32px 0\"><strong>Christine&rsquo;s Promise:</strong> Personal reply within 1 business day. No bots. No call center. Honest answers &mdash; even if it&rsquo;s &ldquo;not yet.&rdquo; Call or text <a href=\"tel:3037094262\" style=\"color:inherit;font-weight:700;\">303-709-4262</a>.</div>\r\n</article>\r\n<!-- VISIBLE FAQ ACCORDION -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"container\" id=\"faqs\" style=\"padding:60px 0; border-top:1px solid var(--line);\">\r\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif; font-size:2rem; color:var(--forest); margin-bottom:32px;\">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>\r\n\r\n<details style=\"border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:20px 0;\"><summary style=\"font-weight:700; font-size:1.1rem; cursor:pointer; color:var(--forest);\">Are rent-to-own homes legit in Colorado?</summary>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:12px;\">Some are, but most online rent-to-own listings for Northern Colorado are either lead-generation traps, pre-foreclosure situations, or expensive corporate programs. Always verify with a local Realtor before any money changes hands.</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details style=\"border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:20px 0;\"><summary style=\"font-weight:700; font-size:1.1rem; cursor:pointer; color:var(--forest);\">How does rent-to-own work in Loveland and Fort Collins?</summary>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:12px;\">A rent-to-own agreement in Loveland or Fort Collins typically involves leasing a home for 1&ndash;3 years with the right or obligation to buy at the end. A portion of your monthly rent goes toward your future down payment.</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details style=\"border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:20px 0;\"><summary style=\"font-weight:700; font-size:1.1rem; cursor:pointer; color:var(--forest);\">Do I need good credit for rent-to-own in Colorado?</summary>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:12px;\">Most legitimate programs require a credit score of at least 580&ndash;620, verifiable income of about 3x the monthly rent, and no recent evictions or bankruptcies.</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details style=\"border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:20px 0;\"><summary style=\"font-weight:700; font-size:1.1rem; cursor:pointer; color:var(--forest);\">What's the difference between lease-option and lease-purchase?</summary>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:12px;\">A lease-option gives you the right but not the obligation to buy. A lease-purchase creates a contractual obligation &mdash; if you can't qualify for a mortgage at the end, you can be sued for breach of contract.</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details style=\"border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:20px 0;\"><summary style=\"font-weight:700; font-size:1.1rem; cursor:pointer; color:var(--forest);\">Can I rent-to-own with bad credit in Northern Colorado?</summary>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:12px;\">Most legitimate programs still require a 580+ credit score. If your credit is lower, the honest answer is that no rent-to-own program will be a good deal for you &mdash; and 12 months of focused credit repair will get you further than a lease-option ever will.</p>\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n<details style=\"border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); padding:20px 0;\"><summary style=\"font-weight:700; font-size:1.1rem; cursor:pointer; color:var(--forest);\">Are there alternatives that get me into a home faster?</summary>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:12px;\">Yes &mdash; and most renters who call about rent-to-own actually qualify for one. CHFA offers down payment assistance grants. USDA loans offer $0 down in much of Weld County. FHA with down payment assistance often requires nothing out of pocket. Take the Quick Check below and I'll tell you exactly which one fits.</p>\r\n</details>\r\n</section>\r\n<!-- VISUAL JOURNEY MAP -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"container\" style=\"padding: 60px 0; background: white; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line)\">\r\n<h2 style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif; font-size:2rem; color:var(--forest); text-align:center; margin-bottom:40px;\">Your Simple 5-Step Path to Homeownership</h2>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; gap:20px; justify-content:center;\">\r\n<div style=\"flex:1; min-width:220px; text-align:center; position:relative;\">\r\n<div style=\"width: 60px; height: 60px; background: #b98e4d; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 0 auto 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; box-shadow: 0 4px 12px -4px rgba(185,142,77,.4)\">1</div>\r\n\r\n<h4 style=\"margin:8px 0 4px;\">Take the 60-Second Quick Check</h4>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:0.95rem;color:#5a625d;\">Answer a few questions about your situation</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"flex:1; min-width:220px; text-align:center; position:relative;\">\r\n<div style=\"width: 60px; height: 60px; background: #b98e4d; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 0 auto 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; box-shadow: 0 4px 12px -4px rgba(185,142,77,.4)\">2</div>\r\n\r\n<h4 style=\"margin:8px 0 4px;\">I Personally Review Your Info</h4>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:0.95rem;color:#5a625d;\">No bots &mdash; I look at your real options</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"flex:1; min-width:220px; text-align:center; position:relative;\">\r\n<div style=\"width: 60px; height: 60px; background: #b98e4d; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 0 auto 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; box-shadow: 0 4px 12px -4px rgba(185,142,77,.4)\">3</div>\r\n\r\n<h4 style=\"margin:8px 0 4px;\">See Your Best Paths</h4>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:0.95rem;color:#5a625d;\">Rent-to-own, $0-down USDA/CHFA, or credit repair plan</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"flex:1; min-width:220px; text-align:center; position:relative;\">\r\n<div style=\"width: 60px; height: 60px; background: #b98e4d; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 0 auto 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; box-shadow: 0 4px 12px -4px rgba(185,142,77,.4)\">4</div>\r\n\r\n<h4 style=\"margin:8px 0 4px;\">Choose What Fits You</h4>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:0.95rem;color:#5a625d;\">I explain every option honestly</p>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"flex:1; min-width:220px; text-align:center; position:relative;\">\r\n<div style=\"width: 60px; height: 60px; background: #b98e4d; color: white; border-radius: 50%; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; margin: 0 auto 12px; font-size: 1.4rem; font-weight: 700; box-shadow: 0 4px 12px -4px rgba(185,142,77,.4)\">5</div>\r\n\r\n<h4 style=\"margin:8px 0 4px;\">Get Into Your Home</h4>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:0.95rem;color:#5a625d;\">Faster and with less risk than most people expect</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n<!-- QUICK CHECK -->\r\n\r\n<section id=\"quick-check\" style=\"padding: 70px 0; background: #f4ede2\">\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n<div class=\"quick-check-inner\" style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:40px;align-items:start;max-width:1140px;margin:0 auto;\">\r\n<div><span style=\"background: #b98e4d; color: white; padding: 6px 14px; border-radius: 9999px; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 800\">Free &middot; No obligation</span>\r\n\r\n<h2 style=\"font-size:2.4rem;margin:16px 0 12px;\">Your 60-Second Path-to-Homeownership Quick Check</h2>\r\n\r\n<p>Answer a few quick questions and I&rsquo;ll personally email you back within one business day with your real options &mdash; rent-to-own, $0-down programs, or a credit-and-savings game plan. No bots. No call center. Just me.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul style=\"list-style:none;padding:0;\">\r\n\t<li style=\"margin:8px 0;\">✓ Personal reply within 1 business day</li>\r\n\t<li style=\"margin:8px 0;\">✓ No spam, ever &mdash; I hate it too</li>\r\n\t<li style=\"margin:8px 0;\">✓ Honest answer even if it&rsquo;s &ldquo;not yet&rdquo;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-top:24px;font-size:0.9rem;color:#5a625d;\">Most people are surprised by what they actually qualify for.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n<iframe allowfullscreen=\"true\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://form.jotform.com/260648335652057\" style=\"width:100%;min-height:620px;border:none;border-radius:14px;\" title=\"Path to Homeownership Quick Check\"></iframe></div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n<!-- SERVING HIGH-DEMAND POCKETS -->\r\n\r\n<section class=\"container\" style=\"padding:40px 0; border-top:1px solid var(--line); text-align:center;\">\r\n<p style=\"font-size:0.8rem; letter-spacing:1px; color:var(--gold); text-transform:uppercase; font-weight:700;\">Serving High-Demand Pockets Across:</p>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"display:flex; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; gap:10px; margin-top:10px;\"><span style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 5px 15px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.9rem\">Seven Lakes (Loveland)</span> <span style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 5px 15px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.9rem\">Old Town (Fort Collins)</span> <span style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 5px 15px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.9rem\">RainDance (Windsor)</span> <span style=\"background: white; border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 5px 15px; border-radius: 5px; font-size: 0.9rem\">Poudre River Ranch (Greeley)</span></div>\r\n</section>\r\n</main>\r\n<!-- FOOTER -->\r\n\r\n<footer style=\"background: #1f3a2e; color: white; padding: 40px 0; text-align: center\">\r\n<div class=\"container\">\r\n<p style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;font-size:1.4rem;margin:0 0 8px;\">The Little Lady Sells Homes</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Christine Gwinnup &middot; Loveland, CO &middot; 303-709-4262</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"font-size:0.85rem;opacity:0.8;margin-top:16px;\">&copy; 2026 Christine Gwinnup. Equal Housing Opportunity. This page is for informational purposes only and is not legal or financial advice.</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</footer></head></html>\n"
